                  %div
                    %p
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#details"} Details
              %li
                %a{:href => "#in_terms_of_homotopy_limit"} In terms of homotopy limit
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} Simplicial presheaves
            equipped with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            are one model/presentation for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
            on a given
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
          %p
            The fibrant object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar X
            that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi SSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : S^{op} \to SSet
            is weakly equivalent to with respect to this model structure is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stackification"} ∞-stackification
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaves
            are precisely those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-presheaves
            which satisfy a kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            condition.
          %p
            Precsisely what this condition is like for the particular model constituted by simplicial presheaves with the given Jardine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            was worked out in
          %ul
            %li
              Daniel Dugger, Sharon Hollander, Daniel C. Isaksen,
              %em Hypercovers and simplicial presheaves
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0563/"}> web
              )
          %p and
          %ul
            %li
              Toën-Vezzosi,
              %em Segal topoi and stacks over Segal categories
              (
              %a{:href => "https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.1046.508&rep=rep1&type=pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p recalled as corollary 6.5.3.13 in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
          %p The following is a summary of these results.
          %p
            The main point is that the fibrant objects are essentially those simplicial presheaves, which satisfy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            with respect not just to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covers"} covers
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercovers"} hypercovers
          %p
            Localizations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-presheaves
            at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercovers"} hypercovers
            are called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercompletions"} hypercompletions
            in
            %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/papers/highertopoi.pdf#page=534"} section 6.5.3
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
            %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/papers/highertopoi.pdf#page=539"} section 6.5.4
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
            it is argued that it may be more natural
            %em not
            to localize at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercovers"} hypercovers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covers"} covers
            after all.
          %h2#details Details
          %p
            A well-studied class of models/presentations for an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
            is obtained using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            on an ordinary (1-categorical)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, SSet]
            be the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimpSet"} SSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaves
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            Recall from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            that there is the
            %em global
            and the
            %em local
            injective simplicial model structure on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, SSet]
          %p
            According to
            %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/papers/highertopoi.pdf#page=528"} section 6.5.2
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT
            we have:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the full simplicial subcategory on fibrant-cofibrant objects of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi SSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, SSet]
                with respect to the
                %em global
                injective model structure is (the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimpSet"} SSet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
                realization of) the
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi PSh
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(S)
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-presheaves
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %li
              %p
                the full simplicial subcategory on fibrant-cofibrant objects of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi SSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, SSet]
                with respect to the
                %em local
                injective model structure is (the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimpSet"} SSet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
                realization of) the
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi Sh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{Sh}_{(\infty,1)}(S)
                which is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercompletion"} hypercompletion
                of the
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sh
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(S)
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaves
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            Since with respect to the local or global injective model structure all objects are automatically cofibrant, this means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar Sh_{(\infty,1)}(S)
            is the full sub-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-category of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(S)
            on simplicial presheaves which are fibrant with respect to the local injective model structure: these are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            in this model.
          %p
            By the general properties of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localization of an (∞,1)-category
            there should be a class of morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Y \to X
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(S)
            – hence between injective-fibrant objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, PSh(S)]
            – such that the simplicial presheaves representing
            = succeed "-stacks" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
            with respect to these morphisms.
          %p This was worked out in
          %ul
            %li
              D. Dugger, S. Hollander, D. Isaksen,
              %em Hypercovers and simplicial presheaves
              (
              %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu//Dugger-Hollander-Isaksen/hypspre.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p We now describe central results of that article.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in S
              an object in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              regarded as a simplicial presheaf and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \in [S^{op}, SSet]
              a simplicial presheaf on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
              is a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercover"} hypercover
              if it is a
              = succeed "," do
                %em local acyclic fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in S
              and all diagrams
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Λ
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi respectively
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∂
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Lambda^k[n]\otimes V &amp;\to &amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta^n\otimes V &amp;\to&amp;
                    X
                    }
                    \\;\; respectively \;\,
                    \\array{
                    \\partial \Delta^n\otimes V &amp;\to &amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta^n\otimes V &amp;\to&amp;
                    X
                    }
            %p
              there exists a covering
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to V\}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              with respect to the given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              such that for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \to V
              in that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
              the pullback of the abve diagram to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              has a lift
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Λ
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi respectively
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∂
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Lambda^k[n]\otimes U_i &amp;\to &amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;\nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta^n\otimes U_i &amp;\to&amp;
                    X
                    }
                    \\;\; respectively \;\,
                    \\array{
                    \\partial \Delta^n\otimes U_i &amp;\to &amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;\nearrow&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta^n\otimes U_i &amp;\to&amp;
                    X
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verdier+site"} Verdier site
            then every such hypercover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
            has a refinement by a hypercover which is cofibrant with respect to the projective global
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
            we discuss are cofibrant in this sense. These are called
            = succeed "." do
              %em split hypercovers
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu//Dugger-Hollander-Isaksen/hypspre.pdf#page=29"} DHI, def. 9.1
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(S)
              – i.e. the fibrant objects with respect to the projective model structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, SSet]
              – are precisely those objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(S)
              – i.e.
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              = succeed "," do
                %strong satisfy descent for all split hypercovers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Y \to X
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, SSet]
              we have that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [S^{op}, SSet](X,A) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    [S^{op}, SSet](Y,A)
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} weak equivalence of simplicial sets
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              This is
              %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu//Dugger-Hollander-Isaksen/hypspre.pdf#page=3"} DHI, thm 1.3
              formulated in the light of
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu//Dugger-Hollander-Isaksen/hypspre.pdf#page=9"} DHI, lemma 4.4 ii)
          %p
            Notice that by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Yoneda+lemma"} co-Yoneda lemma
            every simplicial presheaf
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : S^{op} \to SSet
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : \Delta^{op}\times S^{op} \to Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted colimit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi colim
                    %mi Δ
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F \simeq colim^\Delta F_\bullet
          %p
            which is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} coend
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Δ
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F \simeq \int^{[n] \in \Delta} \Delta^n \cdot F_n
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_n
            is the Set-valued presheaf of
            = succeed "-cells" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            regarded as an
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSet
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set \hookrightarrow SSet
            = succeed "-weight" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimpSet"} SSet
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in S
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Δ
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F : X \mapsto \int^{[n] \in \Delta} \Delta^n \times F(X)_n
                  \\,.
          %p
            In particular therefore for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi colim
                    %mi Δ
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi lim
                    %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [S^{op}, SSet](X,A) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                  [S^{op}, SSet](colim^\Delta Y_\bullet,A)
                  \\simeq
                  lim^\Delta [S^{op}, SSet](Y_\bullet,A)
                  \\,.
          %p
            With the shorthand notation introduced above the
            %strong descent condition
            finally reads, for all global-injective fibrant simplicial presheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and hypercovers
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi lim
                    %mi Δ
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A(X) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} lim^\Delta A(Y_\bullet)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The right hand here is often denoted
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Desc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Desc(Y_\bullet \to X, A)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi Desc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A(X) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} Desc(Y_\bullet \to X, A)
                  \\,.
          %h2#in_terms_of_homotopy_limit In terms of homotopy limit
          %p
            (expanded version of remark 2.1 in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu//Dugger-Hollander-Isaksen/hypspre.pdf"} DHI
          %p
            Using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield-Kan+map"} Bousfield-Kan map
            every simplicial presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is also weakly equivalent to the weighted limit over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\bullet
            with weight given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo →
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(\Delta/(-)) : \Delta \to SSet
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo •
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi lim
                    %mi Δ
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo •
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  lim^{N(\Delta/(-))} F_\bullet \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                  lim^\Delta F_\bullet
                  \\,.
          %p
            But by the discussion at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\bullet
            (since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\bullet
            is objectwise fibrant, since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_n
            factors through
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set \hookrightarrow SSet
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi holim
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo •
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  holim F_\bullet \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                  F
                  \\,.
          %p
            Often the descent condition is therefore formulated with the cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            replaced by its homotopy limit, whence it reads
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi hocolim
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mo •
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [S^{op}, SSet](X,A) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                  [S^{op}, SSet](hocolim U_\bullet,A)
                  \\,.
          %p
            With
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            global-injective fibrant this is equivalent to
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi holim
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mo •
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [S^{op}, SSet](X,A) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                  holim [S^{op}, SSet](U_\bullet,A)
                  \\,.
          %p Using the notation introduced above this becomes finally
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi holim
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A(X) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} holim A(U_\bullet)
                  \\,.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-sheaf"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                  \-sheaf
